Review the Chinese-to-English translation in this directory for the MPI Buddhist
translation project. Files: source.dj (Chinese source, 214 lines), target.dj (En
glish translation), bilingual.dj (interleaved pairs). Read source.dj and target.
dj fully, line by line. Check: 1) Accuracy — mistranslations, omissions, additio
ns, meaning drift, subject confusion; 2) Buddhist terminology — consistent, stan
dard renderings (e.g. 皈依/refuge, 发心/aspiration, 戒律/precepts, 正见/right vi
ew, 止观/samatha-vipassana, 菩提心/bodhicitta, 出离心/renunciation, 凡夫心/ordin
ary mind, 修学次第/stages of practice); 3) Fluency and register — natural idioma
tic English appropriate to a scholarly Buddhist essay by Master Jiqun (written g
enre, first-person teacher voice, rhetorical questions preserved); 4) Completene
ss — every source paragraph covered, no truncation. CRITICAL: Do NOT modify, cre
ate, or delete any files, and do NOT run any shell commands or edit anything. Re
ad-only review only. Report findings as your final message: organized by severit
y (critical/major/minor), each with source line number, the issue, and a concret
e fix. End with a one-line overall verdict.
TurnBegin(
    user_input='Review the Chinese-to-English translation in this directory for 
the MPI Buddhist translation project. Files: source.dj (Chinese source, 214 line
s), target.dj (English translation), bilingual.dj (interleaved pairs). Read sour
ce.dj and target.dj fully, line by line. Check: 1) Accuracy — mistranslations, o
missions, additions, meaning drift, subject confusion; 2) Buddhist terminology —
consistent, standard renderings (e.g. 皈依/refuge, 发心/aspiration, 戒律/precept
s, 正见/right view, 止观/samatha-vipassana, 菩提心/bodhicitta, 出离心/renunciati
on, 凡夫心/ordinary mind, 修学次第/stages of practice); 3) Fluency and register 
— natural idiomatic English appropriate to a scholarly Buddhist essay by Master 
Jiqun (written genre, first-person teacher voice, rhetorical questions preserved
); 4) Completeness — every source paragraph covered, no truncation. CRITICAL: Do
NOT modify, create, or delete any files, and do NOT run any shell commands or ed
it anything. Read-only review only. Report findings as your final message: organ
ized by severity (critical/major/minor), each with source line number, the issue
, and a concrete fix. End with a one-line overall verdict.'
)
